    "language": "en",
    "statementMarkdown": "The following construction is used for training astronauts: A circle $C_{2}$ of radius $2 R$ rolls along the inside of another, fixed circle $C_{1}$ of radius $n R$, where $n$ is an integer greater than 2 . The astronaut is fastened to a third circle $C_{3}$ of radius $R$ which rolls along the inside of circle $C_{2}$ in such a way that the touching point of the circles $C_{2}$ and $C_{3}$ remains at maximum distance from the touching point of the circles $C_{1}$ and $C_{2}$ at all times (see Figure 3).\n\nHow many revolutions (relative to the ground) does the astronaut perform together with the circle $C_{3}$ while the circle $C_{2}$ completes one full lap around the inside of circle $C_{1}$ ?\n",
